      "description": "Watch Chelsea vs Brighton highlights and goals from Premier League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 30, 2026. The air was thick with anticipation as two of England's most dynamic sides faced off in an afternoon of high-stakes football. Every passage of play seemed to carry the weight of the match, as fans were treated to a display of attacking intent that defied tactical norms. A Lightning Start at the Bridge On August 30, 2026 , the Premier League witnessed a chaotic and clinical opening in the clash between Chelsea and Brighton . The deadlock was broken just 4 minutes in when Romeo Lavia pounced on a loose ball following a mistake by goalkeeper Bart Verbruggen , firing home with his right foot. The home side didn't let up, and by the 14th minute, they had doubled their advantage. Pedro Neto found the back of the net after a precise assist from Morgan Rogers , leaving the visitors reeling from an early double blow. Brighton's Spirited Comeback Despite the early setback, Brighton showcased their trademark resilience and technical quality. In the 32nd minute, Joao Pedro began the fightback, finishing clinically after being set up by Jorrel Hato . The momentum swung violently in favor of the \"Seagulls,\" and just three minutes later, the scores were level. Malick Junior Yalcouye unleashed a stunning right-footed volley that flew into the net, completing a remarkable ten-minute turnaround and ensuring the sides went into the break on equal terms. Twists and the Palmer Factor The second half introduced fresh drama and a touch of misfortune. In the 63rd minute, Chelsea regained the lead in unexpected fashion when Joao Pedro inadvertently sent the ball into his own net during a defensive scramble from a corner. The hosts capitalized on this stroke of luck, and in the 74th minute, Cole Palmer produced a moment of magic. Picking up the ball outside the box, the forward unleashed a pinpoint left-footed strike that beat the keeper to make it 4-2. A Frantic Finish The closing stages were defined by tactical fouls and rising tempers, as Brighton ’s Lewis Dunk , Olivier Boscagli , and Costinha all entered the referee's book. Despite holding a staggering 74% of the possession, the visitors struggled to break through a determined Chelsea defense until the dying embers of the game. In the 6th minute of stoppage time, Pascal Gross headed home a loose ball to bring the score to 4-3, but it proved to be too little, too late as the referee blew the final whistle shortly after."
